# Which cache plan should we ship? {#cache-plan}

Ship the read-through cache: it **halves** read latency at a [typical](typical:measured on one staging host) cost.[](source:bench)

- Reads hit Redis first.[](source:docs)
- Writes stay on the database path.

@answer scope="Order API · read path · staging numbers"
@meta locale=en
@source docs title="Cache design notes" url=https://example.com/cache
@source bench title="Staging benchmark"
@source unused title="Background reading"

## What do the options cost? {#options}

| Criterion | Read-through | Write-behind |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Latency {#latency-row} | 12 ms {good:Faster} | 20 ms {caution} |
| Risk | Stale reads | Lost writes {bad:Data loss} |
| Effort | Low | High |

@facts id=facts
| Owner | Platform team |
| Rollout | One region first |

## How close are we to the limits? {#limits}

@metric id=p99 label="P99 latency" value=180 limit=150 unit=ms typical=true note="Peak hour"

@metric id=capacity label="Capacity" limit=10 unit=requests

@metric id=float label="Error budget" value=0.3 limit=0.1

@metric id=within label="Hit rate" value=80 limit=100 unit=%

## What do we do first? {#first}

1. Deploy the cache behind a flag.
2. Measure the hit rate.

@steps id=rollout
| enable | Enable the flag | Start with 1% of reads. |
| watch | Watch the hit rate | Expect [5 ms](typical:median, one host) reads. |

@callout level=warning title="Before rollout"
| Check the eviction policy. |
| A full cache evicts hot keys. |

- [ ] Confirm the flag default
- [ ] Record the baseline

## What changes in the code? {#code-change}

@diff id=change caption="Read through the cache"
```diff
--- a/src/read.js
+++ b/src/read.js
@@ -1,2 +1,3 @@
-return db.get(key);
+const hit = await cache.get(key);
+return hit ?? db.get(key);
 // done
```

```bash title="Run the cache tests"
npm test -- cache
```

