# How does an order move? {#order-flow}

An order is checked, then paid, then shipped.

@meta locale=en
@source checkout title="Checkout service" url=https://example.com/checkout

## Which steps does an order take? {#steps}

@workflow id=order-path title="Order path"
| lane check | Check |
| lane fulfil | Fulfil |
| cart | Cart | frontend | check | source:checkout |
| verify | Verify stock | backend | check |
| pay | Take payment | backend | fulfil |
| ship | Ship | external | fulfil |
| cart > verify | |
| verify > pay | in stock |
| pay > ship | paid | emphasis |

@steps id=walk
| s-cart | Cart | The customer submits the [cart](node:order-path.cart). | order-path | cart |
| s-verify | Verify stock | Stock is reserved. | order-path | verify |
| s-pay | Take payment | Payment follows the [route](route:order-path.verify~pay). | order-path | | verify~pay |

# 首次访问为什么多一次往返？ {#tls}

浏览器和服务器先交换密钥，再发请求。

@meta locale=zh-CN

